    "turn_idx": 15,
    "turn_text": "Is it fair to say, I suppose New Zealand's had immigration elections as well, but it tends to be the level of legal migration rather than illegal migration that swings votes here. Is it fair to say that from what you've just said, the issues that are driving this campaign, do you feel better off than you were four years ago? With the level of inflation that America has experienced, a lot of people don't feel better off than they were four years ago, because they're not. Same as in New Zealand, people are worse off than they were before the inflation spike. And then also this illegal migration issue, which people really struggle to solve. I mean, Donald Trump struggled to solve it as well. The border wall was not completely built.",
